ilure, and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying, so I don't page the on-call engineer twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_011R3VKcL9vtgCC5GsBfAK5W", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release that was failing. No change-manager approval was needed, because v2.3.0 has a healthy production history.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in every region.\n- **Incident:** SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current healthy state. The create call timed out, but the incident was recorded, so I did not retry and did not open a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health-check failures, and check why the orchestrator halted the first rollback attempt.", "type": "text"}]}]}